  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "**Hotel reflagging** is the process of a hotel **changing its brand affiliation**—for example, moving from one chain to another or becoming independent.[1][3][4]\n\nIn practice, reflagging can be a **simple brand switch** or a **major conversion project**.[2][3] It often involves:\n- replacing branded items such as signage, towels, brochures, and literature[1]\n- updating the hotel’s website, social media, and online listings[1]\n- changing operating systems, standards, and guest-service procedures[3]\n- sometimes completing renovations to meet the new brand’s requirements[2][5]\n\nThe scale depends on the situation. Some properties change mostly the visible branding, while others need significant capital investment, IT integration, and even temporary closure during construction.[2][5]\n\nIf you want, I can also explain **why hotels reflag**, **how the process works step by step**, or the difference between **reflagging, deflagging, and rebranding**.",
